###2026.08.11.10
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.11.10
This development build addresses second-generation JavaScript monoliths by moving shared utility and Docker/VM/Dashboard runtime domains behind bounded modules while preserving their established browser and CommonJS compatibility APIs.
### Shared JavaScript boundaries
- Refactor: Split normalization, preferences, ordering, import/export transfer, and runtime-rule logic out of `folderviewplus.utils.js` into five focused foundation modules.
- Refactor: Split runtime primitives, diagnostics, and controls out of `docker.runtime.shared.js` into three shared modules used by Docker, VM, and Dashboard surfaces.
- Compatibility: Retain the complete 49-name utility facade and the extensible shared runtime namespace used by later feature modules.
### Enforcement and regression coverage
- Quality: Reduce `folderviewplus.utils.js` from 2,054 to 88 lines and `docker.runtime.shared.js` from 1,511 to 460 lines.
- Quality: Add eight browser-module ownership contracts, explicit page load-order contracts, dependency metadata, and ratcheted file budgets for every extracted module.
- Reliability: Add Phase 7 facade and load-order regression coverage, update existing owner-location tests, and exercise the decomposed modules through browser fixtures and runtime-performance budgets.
- Security: Refresh the CSP readiness inventory for 207 scanned first-party files while retaining zero inline events, inline scripts, and style attributes.


###2026.08.11.09
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.11.09
This development build completes the PHP decomposition phase by moving server domains behind enforced request-scoped modules while preserving every public endpoint, request guard, response shape, and compatibility function name.
### PHP compatibility boundaries
- Refactor: Split release metadata, durable storage, theme workspace and GitHub import, environment transfer, backup scheduling and snapshots, folder rules and mutations, Docker ordering, custom-icon storage, and runtime information out of `server/lib.php`.
- Refactor: Split diagnostics redaction, integrity collection, summary modeling, and support-bundle assembly out of `server/lib.diagnostics.php`.
- Refactor: Keep `server/upload_custom_icon.php` as a thin compatibility dispatcher backed by separate foundation, validation, and action modules.
- Reliability: Preserve the exact 30-endpoint API manifest and all 276 core, 74 diagnostics, and 56 custom-icon public function names.
### Enforcement and regression coverage
- Quality: Reduce `server/lib.php` from 7,556 to 2,649 lines, `server/lib.diagnostics.php` from 2,923 to 257 lines, and `server/upload_custom_icon.php` from 1,481 to 37 lines.
- Quality: Add 19 server-module ownership contracts with loader validation, exact function-inventory hashes, dependency metadata, and ratcheted file budgets.
- Reliability: Add executable facade-loading tests plus endpoint-manifest, backup, storage, diagnostics, Docker ordering, theme, runtime-information, and custom-icon regression coverage for the new ownership paths.
- Security: Refresh the CSP readiness inventory for 199 scanned first-party files while retaining zero inline events, inline scripts, and style attributes.


###2026.08.11.08
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.11.08
This development build finishes the current Settings and Setup Wizard decomposition phase by moving search state, local persistence, and review modeling behind enforced module boundaries without changing saved preferences or setup behavior.
