###2026.08.10.02
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.10.02
This stable release promotes every validated development change since stable `2026.07.24.13`.
### Runtime architecture and maintainability
- Performance: Split Settings startup into a small first-paint foundation and an interaction/idle-deferred workspace while preserving strict dependency order.
- Reliability: Add per-module startup timing, bounded timeouts, failed-module identification, version evidence, and one resumable retry instead of allowing a stalled asset to leave Settings blank.
- Maintenance: Extract focused modules for remote retrieval, Docker layout geometry, container normalization, download diagnostics, support-bundle comparison, and Settings workspace behavior.
- Maintenance: Ratchet architecture budgets for browser globals, inline actions, and the largest JavaScript, CSS, PHP, and page files.
- Quality: Expand JavaScript coverage thresholds, PHPStan analysis, dead-code checks, localization migration budgets, and deterministic browser/runtime performance contracts.
- Docs: Add current architecture, browser-support, Docker compatibility, diagnostics privacy, package storage, security, and release-integrity guidance.
### Docker API compatibility and first-render stability
- Feature: Add operation-level GraphQL capability discovery for Docker queries, mutations, subscriptions, arguments, return types, and deprecation metadata.
- Feature: Add a hybrid legacy/GraphQL provider that prefers schema-confirmed reads and statistics while leaving current Unraid lifecycle actions authoritative.
- Compatibility: Normalize GraphQL, PHP, and DOM container records into one immutable model with stable runtime identity and metadata.
- Reliability: Fall back safely when GraphQL is unavailable or incomplete, reject stale responses, abort owned requests, and dispose subscriptions across navigation.
- Feature: Add targeted single-container reconciliation and aggregate update, orphan, rebuild, and port-conflict health checks.
- Privacy: Keep Docker logs on demand and export only aggregate compatibility and health evidence in sanitized diagnostics.
- Fix: Reserve WebUI, console, and log action slots during the first preview render so later metadata cannot shift existing controls.
- Fix: Reconcile Docker preview actions in place and provide lightweight WebUI capability hints before full template hydration.
- Fix: Measure localized folder/status content before showing rows and use a schema-, algorithm-, and content-aware Application-column width cache.
- Diagnostics: Record privacy-safe first-render timing, width stages, action-slot availability, row motion, and within-row action displacement.
- Maintenance: Track upstream Unraid Docker schema, API releases, source-gate changes, and activation announcements without enabling prerelease organizer mutations.
### Security update sequence
- Security: Require explicit mutation markers, trusted same-origin context, per-install request tokens, and fail-closed token availability for protected POST actions.
- Security: Add target-bound, short-lived, one-time mutation nonces, transaction replay rejection, bounded endpoint rate limits, and standards-based retry guidance.
- Security: Enforce endpoint method, action, content-type, request-size, and parameter contracts through the shared API manifest.
- Security: Restrict folder identifiers, prototype-sensitive keys, external links, WebUI navigation, popup names, image URLs, and localized rich text before browser or server use.
- Security: Preflight icon archives for traversal, links, special files, depth, count, per-file size, total size, and expected top-level content before private staged activation.
- Security: Constrain durable writes to approved roots, reject symbolic-link path components, and use restrictive atomic temporary files.
- Security: Replace direct shell execution with one allowlisted, shell-free `proc_open` boundary using fixed executable candidates, argument arrays, output caps, and timeouts.
- Security: Replace plugin-owned inline event handlers with a delegated declarative bridge that does not use `eval` or the `Function` constructor.
- Security: Reject executable managed-theme content, remote imports, external network URLs, and HTML data URLs before persistence or rendering.
- Security: Generate and verify a deterministic SHA-256 runtime-integrity manifest covering expected files, permissions, and unexpected executable content.
- Security: Record a bounded HMAC hash-chained security audit containing only sanitized action metadata, random trace IDs, status, and timestamps.
- Security: Pin all external GitHub Actions, expand CodeQL coverage, add dependency-review and OpenSSF Scorecard workflows, and maintain high-severity merge protection.
- Privacy: Disable live-system artifact capture by default and prevent CI/release workflows from uploading private Unraid screenshots, URLs, logs, or support data.
- Security: Publish SHA-256 package and icon-pack digests, a complete CycloneDX runtime/workflow SBOM, GitHub OIDC provenance, and SBOM attestations.
- Diagnostics: Surface sanitized runtime-integrity and security-audit health without exposing payloads, names, paths, addresses, tokens, or nonces.
### Folder interaction reliability
- Fix: Route Docker and VM folder icon, name, edit, expand, and menu behavior through an idempotent shared delegated-action controller.
- Fix: Prepare folder context menus during the capture phase so the first folder-icon click opens the newly attached Unraid menu.
- Fix: Retain the newest Pin or Unpin intent while an earlier preference save is still in flight.
- Fix: Update visible Pin/Unpin order, badge, and menu state immediately while preserving revision checks, server verification, rollback, and stale-render protection.
- Reliability: Remove duplicate handlers during repeated navigation and release owned capture/delegated listeners during teardown.
- Diagnostics: Treat the shared folder-action controller as required and ignore only the exact managed icon-pack activation record during runtime-integrity scans.
### Diagnostics, exports, and user experience
- UI/UX: Remove lower-right completion popups from Settings and Dashboard while preserving nonvisual live-region announcements and actionable modal failures.
- Reliability: Keep destructive-action recovery in Advanced > Recovery and retain inline tree-move Undo/Redo controls instead of short-lived popup Undo actions.
- Diagnostics: Add bounded privacy-safe download lifecycles for Docker, VM, and plugin configuration exports without claiming that a browser save completed.
- UI/UX: Show missing-download and retry controls beside export actions, retaining the latest payload briefly so a direct user click can retry with fresh activation.
- Privacy: Exclude export names, configuration contents, workload identities, paths, addresses, and identifiers from download diagnostics and support bundles.
- Reliability: Replace generic bootstrap failures with a shared startup-incident model across Settings, Docker, VM, Dashboard, and Folder Editor.
- Diagnostics: Preserve the latest sanitized startup incident for 24 hours in browser-session storage, including module outcomes and recovery history after navigation or successful recovery.
- Accessibility: Add plain-language startup summaries, visible reference codes, keyboard focus, live-region semantics, focus indicators, reduced-motion behavior, and translated recovery actions.
- Privacy: Sanitize copied support codes and downloadable startup reports by default, reducing URLs to routes and masking private hosts, addresses, and filesystem paths.
- Diagnostics: Add a privacy-safe command-line comparison tool for sanitized support bundles and more precise browser/runtime evidence for troubleshooting.
### Localization and accessibility
- Fix: Activate the canonical resolved browser catalog so Unraid `zh_CN` sessions use complete Simplified Chinese instead of falling back to English.
- Localization: Add complete Arabic, Bengali, Catalan, Croatian, Danish, Hungarian, Latvian, Norwegian Bokmål, and Traditional Chinese catalogs.
- Compatibility: Map native Unraid regional identifiers for all supported Chinese variants and the expanded language set to canonical plugin locales.
- Accessibility: Enable production RTL direction for Arabic and validate locale selection, rendered translations, direction changes, and pseudo-locale restoration in real browsers.
- Localization: Apply a pinned build-time Taiwan normalization profile for independently translated Traditional Chinese without adding an Unraid runtime dependency.
- Quality: Enforce locale-specific plural forms, placeholders, markup order, catalog completeness, HTML safety, and exact link targets across all 27 locales.
- Quality: Make startup-banner translation calls statically discoverable so strict unused-key validation covers every early recovery message.
- Localization: Advance the catalog to revision `2026.08.10.1` with 2,060 complete messages per locale, including startup recovery vocabulary.
### Release, CI, and supply-chain reliability
- Reliability: Prevent package-version reuse by considering manifests, archives, branches, remote state, and tags during allocation.
- Reliability: Make package provenance content-addressed and normalize tar ownership, timestamps, ordering, and permissions for byte-identical Windows/WSL/Linux builds.
- Quality: Compare two isolated packages and the checked-in archive byte for byte during deterministic-build validation.
- Reliability: Require stable releases to pass configured live Unraid version, browser, and theme matrices in addition to deterministic fixtures.
- Test: Add weekly cross-browser validation in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit plus expanded mobile, RTL, accessibility, theme, interaction, security, and extreme-load coverage.
- Maintenance: Add remote raw manifest/archive/checksum verification, archive retention auditing, release provenance, stable comparison links, and bounded commit history.
- Fix: Correct Linux CI dependency installation, cross-platform path handling, Settings diagnostics initialization, stylesheet budgets, WebKit theme contrast, and canonical line-ending packaging drift found while monitoring dev releases.
- Regression guard: Cover GraphQL capability/fallback behavior, runtime disposal, first-frame geometry, mutation security, filesystem/process boundaries, folder interactions, downloads, localization, startup recovery, packaging, and publication workflows.


###2026.08.10.01
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.10.01
### Recoverable startup diagnostics
- Reliability: Replace generic bootstrap failures with a shared startup-incident model across Settings, Docker, VM, Dashboard, and the folder editor.
- Reliability: Add a bounded **Try loading again** action that resumes the Settings loader from the failed module, cache-busts only that retry, and keeps reload available as the safe fallback.
- Diagnostics: Record module stage, outcome, duration, asset version, retry state, resource timing, last completed step, and recovery history without exposing private runtime values.
- Diagnostics: Preserve the latest startup incident for 24 hours in browser-session storage so a sanitized support bundle can include the failure after navigation or successful recovery.
- Privacy: Make copied support codes and downloadable startup reports sanitized by default, reducing URLs to routes and masking private hosts, addresses, and filesystem paths.
- Accessibility: Add plain-language failure summaries, visible reference codes, keyboard focus, live-region semantics, focus indicators, reduced-motion handling, and translated recovery actions.
- Localization: Add the startup recovery vocabulary to all 27 supported locales and advance the complete 2,060-message catalog to revision `2026.08.10.1`.
- Performance: Stage Settings workspace modules after an idle or interaction opportunity and apply a 12-second per-module timeout so stalled assets fail predictably instead of leaving a blank page.
- Maintenance: Document the incident lifecycle, module-loader telemetry, support workflow, and recovery behavior; refresh CSP readiness metadata and deterministic browser contracts.
- Regression guard: Add fault-injection coverage for failed and stalled assets, one-shot recovery, CSP classification, sanitized persistence, support-bundle redaction, Settings failure presentation, and cross-surface bootstrap wiring.


###2026.08.06.02
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.06.02
### Expanded Unraid language coverage
- Localization: Add complete 2,049-message catalogs for Arabic, Bengali, Catalan, Croatian, Danish, Hungarian, Latvian, Norwegian Bokmål, and Traditional Chinese across Docker, VM, Dashboard, Settings, diagnostics, setup, import, and legacy surfaces.
- Compatibility: Map Unraid language identifiers to canonical plugin locales, including `ar_AR`, `bn_BN`, `bn_BD`, `ca_CA`, `da_DA`, `hr_HR`, `hu_HU`, `lv_LV`, `no_NO`, `nb_NO`, `zh_TW`, `zh_HK`, `zh_MO`, and `zh_Hant`.
- Accessibility: Activate Arabic with RTL document direction and add browser coverage for locale selection, rendered translations, direction changes, and pseudo-locale restoration.
- Localization: Add an independently translated `zh-Hant` catalog and apply a pinned, build-time Taiwan phrase normalization profile without adding a runtime dependency to the Unraid package.
- Quality: Enforce locale-specific plural requirements for Arabic, Croatian, Czech, Latvian, Polish, Romanian, Russian, and Ukrainian while preserving placeholders, markup order, and exact link targets.
- Maintenance: Add explicit scaffolding and targeted refinement options so future catalog maintenance can fill missing root and namespaced messages without silently rewriting accepted translations.
- Regression guard: Expand unit and real-browser coverage for all 27 shipped locales, canonical Unraid aliases, native locale labels, RTL behavior, catalog completeness, HTML safety, and deterministic catalog generation.
- Docs: Document all active locale mappings, Arabic RTL behavior, Traditional Chinese normalization, and the current translation-maintenance workflow.
- Security: Pin the development-only `opencc-js` translation-normalization tool, refresh the complete SBOM, and update the lockfile to resolve the reported high-severity transitive `brace-expansion` advisory.


###2026.08.06.01
## FolderView Plus 2026.08.06.01
### Chinese locale compatibility
- Fix: Activate the canonical resolved catalog in the browser so Unraid `zh_CN` sessions render the complete Simplified Chinese interface instead of falling back to English.
