- Regression guard: Added an initialization-order test covering every normalizer passed into the Filter and View state store so later declarations cannot reintroduce a temporal-dead-zone failure.


###2026.07.22.10
- Refactor: Moved Filter and View setting definitions, type coercion, persisted UI state, range-control bindings, and Docker/VM/Dashboard folder ordering behind shared typed modules instead of duplicated monolith logic.
- Reliability: Added explicit page lifecycle teardown for deferred previews, observers, timers, host adapters, and settings controllers so repeated page navigation cannot retain stale runtime work.
- Compatibility: Formally tracked `performanceMode`, `privacyMaskContainerIps`, and legacy folder regex compatibility. New integrations should use `performanceProfile`, `privacyMaskLocalIps`, and Advanced Auto-Rules respectively; existing saved values remain supported.
- Maintenance: Added authoritative settings, architecture/global, module lifecycle, and deprecation registries with CI guards that reject undeclared controls, contract drift, global collisions, and removed no-op settings.
- Fix: Centralized custom-order cursor removal so a missing Docker or VM member can no longer remove the final unrelated order entry.
- Quality: Replaced brittle implementation-text assertions with executable registry, state-store, ordering, deferred-preview, lifecycle, and deprecation tests while retaining the complete repository regression suite.


