###2026.07.21.26
- Performance: Added one bounded, passive runtime telemetry service for Docker, VMs, Dashboard, Settings, and the modern folder editor with no new bootstrap requests.
- Diagnostics: Support bundles now include privacy-safe timing percentiles, rendering milestones, DOM size, mutation volume, FolderView asset requests, long tasks, and optional heap measurements for visited surfaces.
- Reliability: Action timing is collected outside debug mode, histories remain capped, duplicate Settings/editor visibility samples are prevented, and the export collector remains inside established asset budgets.
- Accessibility: Dashboard Docker and VM folder headers now support Enter and Space, synchronize `aria-expanded` with their controlled member panels, and show a clear keyboard focus ring.
- Accessibility: Decorative folder icons are excluded from assistive output, the Dashboard quick-action group uses localized labeling, and shared disclosure/loading primitives support focus visibility and reduced-motion preferences.
- Quality: Replaced the obsolete nested Dashboard toggle button, removed 34 unnecessary `!important` declarations, ratcheted the CSS-debt ceiling to 1,310, refreshed all 18 locale catalogs, and added unit and browser regressions.


###2026.07.21.22
- Feature: Added complete VM lifecycle reconciliation for native Start, Stop, Pause, Resume, Restart, Hibernate, Wake, Force Stop, and console-start actions.
- Performance: VM actions now update member rows, folder totals, state colors, and menus incrementally without rebuilding the native VM table when runtime state settles normally.
- Reliability: Added generation-aware bounded polling, stale-action cancellation, batch reconciliation for folder and custom actions, and one native refresh fallback when a VM cannot reach its expected state.
- Fix: VM context menus now reflect the current runtime state after lifecycle actions, and lifecycle cleanup restores native action, support, and menu icons without leaving stale spinners or colors.
- Fix: Corrected custom VM Stop actions to send Unraid's native `domain-stop` request.
- Diagnostics: Added persisted, sanitized VM lifecycle events, pending-action state, fallback counts, and host-adapter snapshots to support bundles.
- Test: Added unit and browser fixtures covering VM Stop/Start, Pause/Resume, native menu correction, folder summary updates, icon cleanup, stale generations, and fallback behavior.


###2026.07.21.21
- Refactor: Centralized Unraid Dashboard `loadlist` and `DashboardApps.php` integration behind one idempotent, generation-aware Dashboard host adapter.
- Reliability: Dashboard refreshes now ignore stale native-row responses and permit only one folder-grouping render per active host generation.
- Refactor: Extracted Dashboard runtime icon/state reconciliation and expanded-folder persistence from the main Dashboard script into reusable production modules.
- Diagnostics: Added Dashboard host snapshots and structured `nativeRowsLoaded`, `foldersGrouped`, and `runtimeActionCompleted` lifecycle events.
- Test: Added host-adapter, stale-generation, persisted-state, and module-loading regression coverage, and changed the lifecycle browser fixture to exercise the production runtime-surface controller.
- Quality: Returned the shared UI-debt metric to its approved baseline without changing Dashboard quick-action sizing.


###2026.07.21.20
- Quality: Added a full browser-driven Dashboard container lifecycle fixture using realistic Unraid card markup and the production host-adapter and reconciliation modules.
- Quality: The fixture verifies Stop and Start state convergence, folder aggregate totals, canonical red and green status icons, complete spinner cleanup, and live context-menu action correction.
- Quality: Added Started only coverage across runtime transitions, rapid Stop-to-Start reconciliation, duplicate hook binding protection, and the one-time native refresh fallback for stale Start snapshots.
- Compatibility: Validated the complete fixture suite in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with 66 passing browser checks and no failures.


###2026.07.21.19
- Fix: Dashboard container context menus now resolve Start, Stop, Pause, and Resume availability from the latest reconciled runtime cache instead of the stale inline state captured when the widget first rendered.
- Fix: A container stopped from an expanded Dashboard folder immediately offers Start when its menu is opened again; stopped containers no longer continue offering Stop and Pause.
- Diagnostics: Dashboard lifecycle telemetry now records when a context menu was corrected from current runtime state, including sanitized running, paused, and autostart flags.
- Quality: Added Dashboard wiring and runtime-adapter regressions covering a stopped container whose original native menu payload still claims it is running.


###2026.07.21.18
- Fix: Dashboard container Start actions now fall back to one canonical native widget refresh when incremental runtime reconciliation does not reach the running state within 2.5 seconds.
- Fix: Exhausted lifecycle reconciliation always restores captured card icons before the fallback, preventing indefinite refresh spinners even when the incremental snapshot remains stale.
- Diagnostics: Support bundles now include sanitized Dashboard lifecycle telemetry with each observed state, reconciliation outcome, busy-icon count, and icon-class snapshot; container identities are hashed in sanitized exports.
- Reliability: Dashboard lifecycle completion is generation-scoped and finalized exactly once, preventing stale Stop or Start attempts from triggering duplicate refreshes.
- Quality: Added regression coverage for successful Start convergence, exhausted Start fallback, complete icon cleanup, telemetry persistence, and support-bundle redaction.


###2026.07.21.17
- Fix: Dashboard Start, Stop, Pause, Resume, and Restart actions now restore every native card icon after Unraid applies its temporary busy spinner classes across the card.
- Fix: Running, paused, and stopped member status glyphs now use Unraid's canonical green, orange, and red state colors after incremental reconciliation.
- Reliability: FolderView Plus snapshots the native icon-class contract before lifecycle actions, preserving WebUI, console, and menu icons instead of leaving them animated or altering their original glyphs.
- Quality: Expanded Dashboard lifecycle regression coverage to verify pre-action surface capture, complete busy-state cleanup, and canonical runtime color restoration.


###2026.07.21.16
- Fix: Dashboard container status icons now clear stale Unraid started/stopped tone classes and inline color or animation styles after lifecycle actions.
- Fix: Extra transient spinner nodes are removed while preserving the canonical `load-*` status icon required for subsequent Start and Stop actions.
- Reliability: Member status text and icons now restore a complete final runtime surface instead of retaining host busy-state presentation details.
- Quality: Expanded Dashboard lifecycle regression coverage for stale colors, inline animation, duplicate spinners, and canonical icon preservation.


###2026.07.21.15
- Fix: Dashboard container and folder status icons now clear Unraid's temporary lifecycle spinner classes after Start, Stop, Pause, Resume, or Restart completes.
- Reliability: Incremental Dashboard reconciliation now restores the final runtime icon and removes stale busy state without rebuilding the folder widget.
- Quality: Added regression coverage for clearing host spinner classes from both member and aggregate folder status icons.


###2026.07.21.14
- Fix: Dashboard folder members and aggregate counts now reconcile from stopped back to started after Docker lifecycle actions without requiring a page refresh.
- Performance: Dashboard lifecycle actions keep the grouped folder DOM mounted and use bounded, state-aware runtime refreshes that stop as soon as the requested container state is observed.
- Reliability: Delayed Docker state propagation is followed for up to seven seconds, and a newer lifecycle action cancels stale follow-up work from the previous action.
- Quality: Added regression coverage for delayed start propagation and consecutive stop-to-start transitions while preserving the existing Docker-page reconciliation contract.
- Quality: Icon-pack and package-source content hashing is now deterministic across Linux and Windows Git Bash, preventing false asset-change failures during dev packaging.

###2026.07.21.13
- Fix: Dashboard `Started only` now hides stopped Docker and VM members inside expanded and collapsed folders, hides fully inactive folders, and preserves parent folders with active nested descendants.
- Performance: Dashboard running-only changes now reconcile member and folder visibility in place after toggle, expansion, and live runtime updates instead of rebuilding the complete widget.
- Quality: Added fixture-based Docker and VM coverage for mixed states, paused members, collapsed storage, nested folders, live state changes, and restoring `All Apps`.

###2026.07.21.12
- UI/UX: Increased the Settings Activity Center label to 1.1rem for improved readability.

###2026.07.21.11
- Performance: Settings now retrieves saved Docker and VM folders and preferences through one combined configuration snapshot and paints both tables from a single request, while retaining automatic per-type and legacy request fallbacks for mixed-version installs.
- Performance: Replaced the Diagnostics support-preview full bundle build with a lightweight contract-only endpoint; full host discovery, history collection, redaction, and browser telemetry now run only when a report is copied or exported.
- Diagnostics: Split Settings performance telemetry into configuration first paint, Docker runtime hydration, VM runtime hydration, full manual refresh, and Diagnostics refresh measurements with individual budgets.
- Diagnostics: Persisted bounded performance samples in browser storage for 24 hours across refreshes while limiting health evaluation to the latest 30 minutes so stale timings cannot create current warnings.
- Performance: Preference changes are applied optimistically and coalesced for 160ms; no-op saves no longer rewrite flash state, and display-only changes skip full recovery backups, order reconciliation, and synchronous audit-history writes.
- Reliability: Ordering, rule, start-order, folder-default, import-preset, and backup-schedule changes retain revision checks, atomic last-good writes, full recovery checkpoints, and mutation audit records; repeated checkpoints reuse one recent backup for 30 seconds.
- Quality: Added combined-snapshot, fallback, endpoint-manifest, recovery-classification, persistent telemetry, and lightweight-preview regressions; Chromium UI fixtures and small, normal, and extreme runtime performance budgets pass.

###2026.07.21.10
- Fix: The Settings blank-page watchdog now recognizes the intentional loading shell during its early check, preventing false `FVPLUS-SET-BLANK-001` errors on slower refreshes while retaining the later stalled-bootstrap warning.
- Performance: Removed passive theme-resolution and reflow events from the server diagnostics mutation path so initial styling no longer launches a burst of competing HTTP requests.
- Performance: Theme token application now skips unchanged CSS properties and attributes, breaking the MutationObserver feedback loop that repeatedly re-rendered Settings during startup.
- Performance: The full support-bundle preview is no longer generated on every Settings page load; its code remains ready and the data hydrates on demand when the Advanced Diagnostics tab is actually opened.
- Reliability: Diagnostics preview hydration is deduplicated and cached briefly so repeated Diagnostics navigation cannot start overlapping support-bundle requests.
- Quality: Added regressions for loading-shell watchdog behavior, startup request suppression, on-demand Diagnostics hydration, and idempotent theme-token application.


###2026.07.21.09
- Performance: Settings now loads saved Docker and VM folder configuration through a runtime-free snapshot path, so folder rows no longer wait for Docker inspection or libvirt discovery.
- Performance: Docker and VM runtime details hydrate independently in the background, preventing a slow VM response from delaying Docker folders while retaining complete refresh semantics for recovery and diagnostics actions.
- UI/UX: Added a compact first-paint loading shell and reveal the Settings workspace only after the saved mode, tab, folders, and preferences are applied, eliminating the raw Advanced-page flash during startup.
- UI/UX: Folder status and signal cells show a neutral loading or unavailable state until live runtime data arrives instead of briefly reporting members as stopped.
- Fix: Deferred empty-folder, health, update, quick, and status filtering until runtime hydration is complete so rule-populated folders cannot disappear during first paint.
- Reliability: Kept legacy folder, preference, and runtime requests as automatic fallbacks and increased the warm runtime cache window to avoid unnecessary host queries.
- Quality: Added contract and regression coverage proving config-only snapshots never invoke host runtime discovery, first-paint cloaking is present, runtime hydration remains independent, and explicit refresh workflows still wait for complete data.


###2026.07.21.08
- Performance: Reworked Settings startup to load each Docker and VM core state through one coherent runtime snapshot request instead of separate folder, preference, and runtime requests.
- Performance: Docker and VM settings tables now hydrate first and render in one browser pass, avoiding staged first-load painting.
- Performance: Plugin version lookup, update notes, theme workspace data, and active Advanced-tab datasets no longer block the core Settings page from becoming usable.
- Reliability: Preserved the existing preference coordinator, pending-write replay, and metadata revisions when hydrating from a snapshot, with the previous three-request path retained as an automatic compatibility fallback.
- Quality: Added regression coverage for snapshot script ordering, consolidated Settings bootstrap, synchronized first render, non-blocking optional data, and legacy fallback behavior.


###2026.07.21.05
- UI/UX: Replaced the seven Dashboard View options layout buttons with one compact themed dropdown for Docker and VM widgets.
- Reliability: Kept layout changes on the existing verified preference-save and rollback path, with the current saved layout synchronized into the dropdown whenever the popover opens.
- Accessibility: Uses a native select control with a localized accessible label, native keyboard navigation, disabled save state, and existing Escape/focus restoration behavior.
- Test: Updated fixture and live Dashboard smoke coverage to verify all seven options, the current selection, neutral theme styling, persistence, and dropdown-driven layout switching.


###2026.07.21.04
- Fix: Prevented Unraid's global button styles from applying orange text and borders to the Docker and VM Dashboard View options popover.
- UI/UX: Restyled layout, display, reset, and settings controls with neutral theme-token colors while retaining the intentional blue selected-layout and accessible focus states.
