- Docs: Documented the endpoint registry workflow and requirements for adding future APIs and actions.


###2026.07.19.12
# FolderView Plus 2026.07.19.12
- Reliability: Route durable folder maps, preferences, configuration metadata, diagnostics history, backups, rollback snapshots, templates, theme state, request tokens, Unraid autostart state, and custom icon files through one atomic storage service.
- Safety: Write to a sibling temporary file, flush file contents, atomically replace the target, preserve file permissions, clean up failed temp files, and attempt a parent-directory flush where the platform supports it.
- Recovery: Maintain atomic `.lastgood` JSON mirrors, preserve a successful primary commit when its recovery mirror fails, and refuse to restore corrupt last-good data.
- Diagnostics: Carry one trace and transaction ID across browser requests, API responses and errors, backups, rollback snapshots, configuration revisions, activity history, storage status, and sanitized support bundles.
- Fix: Store uploaded and mirrored custom icon bytes through the same durable writer instead of directly moving or copying data into persistent plugin storage.
- Regression guard: Classify every remaining direct PHP file write and fail validation if a new unclassified write bypasses the durable storage boundary.
- Test: Add failure injection for parent creation, read-only flash storage, temp creation and writes, interrupted writes, full disks, file flushes, atomic renames, directory flushes, last-good failures, and corrupt recovery copies.
- Docs: Document which state is durable, which logs and caches remain intentionally disposable, the commit guarantees, and the storage failure-testing contract.


###2026.07.19.11
# FolderView Plus 2026.07.19.11
- Performance: Add required real-browser runtime budgets for small 25-folder/50-member, normal 100-folder/500-member, and extreme 250-folder/2,000-member configurations.
- Test: Measure navigation-to-native-row visibility, one-shot folder grouping, Settings bootstrap, modern folder editor opening, normalized start/stop reconciliation, and Update-All reconciliation in Chromium.
- Regression guard: Enforce DOM node, MutationObserver callback, retained heap after repeated view switching, and bootstrap network-request ceilings alongside runtime timings.
- Quality: Use one warm-up and five fresh-page samples with stable medians, absolute ceilings, tracked baselines, percentage tolerances, and metric-specific noise floors so tiny timing fluctuations do not fail builds.
- Diagnostics: Publish machine-readable JSON and review-friendly Markdown performance reports with every fixture-browser CI artifact.
- Maintenance: Reconcile the static asset baseline with the already-shipped support-bundle telemetry client so the existing size ratchet remains enforceable alongside the new runtime budgets.
- Docs: Document the scenario matrix, budget policy, local benchmark command, baseline review workflow, and failure interpretation.

###2026.07.19.10
# FolderView Plus 2026.07.19.10
- Refactor: Add one shared, theme-aware UI primitive layer for Settings, Docker, VM, Dashboard, and the modern folder editor.
- Feature: Provide reusable modal and action-sheet, confirmation, alert, button and icon button, disclosure, badge, form field and error, dropdown and multiselect, toast and progress, empty-state, and loading-state APIs.
- Accessibility: Give managed dialogs consistent ARIA semantics, initial focus, keyboard focus trapping, Escape and backdrop policies, nested-dialog ordering, live announcements, body scroll locking, and trigger focus restoration.
- UI/UX: Standardize neutral button hover and focus behavior, responsive modal sizing, contained scrolling, mobile safe-area handling, status tones, compact badges, and theme-token surfaces without adding new `!important` overrides.
- Refactor: Route Settings toast/error output and rollback confirmation through the shared UI layer while keeping a compatibility fallback for legacy SweetAlert availability.
- Refactor: Migrate Diagnostics actions from inline event attributes to delegated UI actions and apply shared buttons, empty states, import disclosure bodies, import badges, folder action-sheet controls, and Docker action-bar controls.
- Localization: Add and fully translate seven common modal, notification, loading, and confirmation labels across all 18 shipped locale catalogs, increasing each catalog to 1,944 messages.
- Regression guard: Add a downward-only UI debt budget that prevents first-party `!important` declarations, SweetAlert references, or inline page event handlers from increasing and forbids `!important` inside the primitive stylesheet.
- Test: Add Node contracts and a real Chromium fixture for every primitive family, delegated actions, confirmation results, modal focus and dismissal, toast lifecycle, and deterministic progress updates.
- Docs: Document the shared component API, delegated-action pattern, styling rules, accessibility ownership, and incremental migration policy.


###2026.07.19.08
# FolderView Plus 2026.07.19.08
- Fix: Stop the localization observer from repeatedly translating its own Settings-page text mutations, which left Settings as one uninitialized long page, kept the browser tab spinner active, and could eventually crash the tab.
- Reliability: Make explicit text, HTML, and attribute translation idempotent so the runtime only writes to the DOM when the localized value actually differs.
- Reliability: Track automatically translated text-node output so observer callbacks settle immediately while still allowing later application-driven text changes to be translated.
- Performance: Replace unbounded microtask translation flushes with one animation-frame batch and collapse very large mutation bursts into one bounded document scan, allowing Settings bootstrap timers and rendering to continue normally.
- Quality: Remove the generic jQuery DOM translation fallback from observer-driven paths and retain the explicit, generated-surface translator as the single DOM mutation owner.
- Test: Add a browser stress regression that inserts more than 300 Settings-like localized nodes, verifies initial and dynamic translation, proves a timer heartbeat is not starved, and confirms translation counts stop changing after the UI settles.


###2026.07.19.07
# FolderView Plus 2026.07.19.07
- Localization: Complete actual localization coverage for the remaining 1,564 initial and runtime-written legacy UI messages, increasing every shipped locale from 373 to 1,937 translated catalog messages.
- Localization: Ship the complete generated surface in Czech, German, Spanish, French, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Dutch, Polish, Brazilian Portuguese, European Portuguese, Romanian, Russian, Swedish, Turkish, Ukrainian, and Simplified Chinese.
- Feature: Translate legacy page text, placeholders, titles, accessibility labels, dynamically inserted UI, and parameterized live-state messages without requiring each legacy renderer to be rewritten.
- Reliability: Preserve `$1`, `$2`, and other runtime parameters through translation generation so names, counts, progress values, and import results cannot be interpreted as currency or lost.
- Reliability: Load the generated `legacy-surface` namespace on every localized plugin page and retain English fallback behavior when an individual catalog asset cannot load.
- Performance: Index exact and parameterized source phrases once, batch MutationObserver updates, and collapse nested mutation roots before translating dynamic UI.
- Diagnostics: Replace the previous 1,588-candidate localization backlog with a zero-uncovered contract and report the 1,564 automatically bound messages in runtime and support diagnostics.
- Quality: Add a deterministic localization surface builder with stable content-addressed keys, existing-translation reuse, request timeouts, progress checkpoints, and placeholder-integrity enforcement.
- Regression guard: Remove the permissive per-file hard-coded-string ceiling; source changes now fail validation until every detected user-facing phrase has a current catalog entry in all 18 locales.
- Test: Add source-to-catalog, locale-completeness, parameter-integrity, mandatory-loader, and real Chromium coverage for initial, attributed, ignored user data, parameterized, and dynamically inserted translations.
- Docs: Document the generated localization workflow, zero-debt validation model, parameter protection, and the fact that installed plugins never contact a translation service.


