###2026.07.15.05
### Instant preference saving
- Feature: Added a shared optimistic preference-save coordinator so Docker, VM, Dashboard, Settings, privacy, folder order, pin, expansion, and auto-rule changes update the interface immediately.
- Performance: Coalesced rapid edits into a single patch per preference type and serialized writes to avoid redundant requests and out-of-order saves.
- UI/UX: Added clear Saved, Saving, and Sync pending status feedback in Settings without blocking normal interaction.
### Reliability and recovery
- Fix: Persisted unsent preference changes in a local outbox so refreshes, navigation, brief network outages, and browser restarts no longer discard pending edits.
- Fix: Added revision-aware conflict recovery that refreshes the server state, reapplies the pending patch, and retries without rolling back the visible interface.
- Fix: Synchronized saved preference changes across browser tabs while preventing duplicate server writes.
- Fix: Restricted automatic retries to transient request failures and retained permanent failures for an intentional later retry.
- Fix: Recursively merged nested preference patches on the server while continuing to replace ordered arrays atomically.
- Fix: Coalesced rapid preference backup checkpoints so a burst of saves retains one useful pre-change snapshot without excessive filesystem work.
### Diagnostics and quality
- Diagnostics: Added aggregate preference-save health, queue, retry, conflict, and latency details to sanitized support bundles without exporting preference values.
- Quality: Added regression coverage for optimistic updates, request coalescing, serialized writes, durable reload recovery, conflict rebasing, cross-tab convergence, nested server merges, backup coalescing, retry classification, request status propagation, and sanitized telemetry.


###2026.07.15.04
- Fix: Keep the Docker privacy toggle enabled across refreshes and Unraid tab navigation with browser-durable state and background server reconciliation.
- Privacy: Mask native Container IP, Container Port, and LAN IP:Port values according to the granular Docker privacy settings.
- Privacy: Synchronize the Docker privacy toggle between open browser tabs without exposing container details.
- Quality: Add regression coverage for durable privacy state and native Docker column masking.


###2026.07.15.03
- Fix: Persist the Docker-page privacy toggle immediately so its enabled state survives refreshes and navigation.
- Fix: Save Dashboard privacy mask options through the optimistic partial-preference path so checkbox changes apply reliably without overwriting unrelated preferences.
- Privacy: Mask container icons inside folder row previews as well as expanded native container rows.
- Quality: Add regression coverage for privacy preference saves, persisted toggle response validation, and folder row-preview masking.


###2026.07.15.02
### Configuration Safety
- Feature: Added versioned metadata sidecars for Docker and VM folders and preferences while preserving the existing configuration-file format.
- Fix: Added revision-aware saves so an older editor or browser tab cannot silently overwrite newer folder or preference changes.
- Fix: Serialized configuration mutations behind a shared lock to prevent overlapping writes from losing data.
- Fix: Kept returned preference revisions synchronized when manual folder ordering is reconciled during a save.
### Recovery and Support
- Feature: Added automatic detection and reconciliation for configuration files changed outside FolderView Plus.
- Feature: Added configuration metadata integrity details, revision history, and fingerprints to Diagnostics and sanitized support bundles.
- Feature: Added a Suggested Fixes action that safely rebuilds and reconciles configuration metadata.
- Fix: Made custom-icon metadata atomic and recoverable through a last-good copy.
### Quality
- Quality: Moved Settings table metadata to a canonical schema with generated runtime output and CI drift detection.
- Quality: Hardened release-note parsing so categorized curated notes remain attached to the correct version.
- Test: Added functional regressions covering revisions, stale saves, external edits, recovery, legacy compatibility, diagnostics, support exports, and icon metadata.


