###2026.03.30.15
- Maintenance: Fold docker update state into hydration signature.
- Maintenance: Trim docker update signature helper.
- Fix: Fix docker update hydration rerender.


###2026.03.30.14
- Fix: Preserve Docker `State.Updated` from the hydrated full runtime payload so folder member rows and folder/root-folder summaries stop getting stuck on `up-to-date` while those containers actually have updates available.
- Fix: Keep lightweight `mode=state` refreshes cheap while still carrying forward the most recent known update state instead of dropping it during Docker runtime info merges.
- Regression guard: Assert the Docker runtime info merge prefers `source.info.State.Updated` from the full payload and only falls back to the previous cached value when the lightweight state payload omits it.


###2026.03.30.13
- Fix: Preserve Docker `State.Updated` from the hydrated full runtime payload so folder member rows and folder/root-folder summaries stop getting stuck on `up-to-date` when those containers actually have updates available.
- Fix: Keep lightweight `mode=state` refreshes cheap while still carrying forward the most recent known update state instead of dropping it back to `null` during runtime merges.
- Regression guard: Assert the Docker runtime info merge prefers `source.info.State.Updated` from the full payload and only falls back to the previous cached value when the lightweight state payload omits it.


###2026.03.30.12
- Fix: Restore the Docker page after the collapsed update-summary refactor by resolving advanced-list mode inside the shared folder update-column renderer instead of referencing an out-of-scope runtime variable during bootstrap.
- Fix: Prioritize the dedicated Docker runtime banner host so fatal runtime diagnostics render at the top of the page instead of dropping to the bottom canvas area.
- Regression guard: Assert the shared folder update-column renderer reads Docker advanced mode locally, and assert fatal-banner host resolution honors selector priority for the dedicated Docker banner host.


###2026.03.30.11
- Fix: Reuse one folder update-column renderer across first paint and runtime hydration so collapsed Docker folders and root folders keep surfacing child container updates without regressing the performance budget.
- Fix: Apply the same host-margin row-centering override to VM folder rows so the VM Application column keeps single-row folder content vertically centered like Docker.
- Regression guard: Assert the shared folder update-column renderer is used by both folder creation and collapsed runtime refresh, and assert the VM row CSS clears host bottom-margin drift.


###2026.03.30.10
- Fix: Rebuild collapsed Docker folder update columns from hydrated runtime container data so folder and root-folder rows show `Update ready` when child containers have updates available, even while the branch is collapsed.
- Fix: Keep the collapsed-folder refresh path aligned with the existing `apply update` and `force update` folder actions instead of leaving the folder row stuck on the lightweight first-paint `up-to-date` state.
- Regression guard: Assert the runtime folder-row refresh path owns the update column and refreshes collapsed folder update state from runtime cache without requiring the folder to be expanded.


###2026.03.30.09
- Fix: Restore the modern folder editor bootstrap after the new accent preview swatch change by defining `accentEnabled` and `accentColor` inside `updateLiveSummary()` before that code touches the live preview chips.
- Fix: Keep the new accent swatch in the editor live preview insights without crashing hydration when the modern editor loads.
- Regression guard: Assert that `folder.editor.preview.js` computes the accent values inside `updateLiveSummary()` before updating `#fvSwatchAccent` and `#fvAccentSwatchItem`.


###2026.03.30.08
- UX: Move the modern folder editor accent color picker into the main `Accent color` card so the toggle and bar color stay together instead of appearing as separate settings blocks.
- UX: Add the folder accent color to the editor live preview insights with its own `Accent` swatch, while keeping the live row accent bar preview in sync.
- Regression guard: Assert the merged accent editor layout, the live preview accent swatch wiring, and the shared accent color contract across the modern and fallback editor chrome paths.


###2026.03.30.07
- Fix: Override the Docker folder row wrapper bottom margin to `0 !important` so the host `span.outer` / `.folder-outer` `margin-bottom: 20px` no longer pulls folder rows upward in the Application column.
- Fix: Revert the recent Docker source-row centering helper experiment and keep the original legacy flex centering path instead of measuring and reapplying source-row heights.
- Regression guard: Assert the Docker folder-row margin override is present and that the source-row centering path stays on the stable `applyRowHeight(row, 0)` plus `applyFolderCellCentering(cell, 0)` contract.


###2026.03.30.06
- Fix: Undo the source-row height forcing from the previous build so Docker folder rows no longer balloon vertically or create massive empty spacing in the table.
- Fix: Center the Docker folder content block by clearing stale forced row heights, measuring the natural rendered row height, and applying that measurement only to the folder name cell centering helper.
- Regression guard: Assert that Docker source rows keep the legacy flex layout, clear forced row height first, and do not reapply `applyRowHeight(row, targetHeight)` in the source-row centering path.


###2026.03.30.05
- Fix: Keep the legacy Docker folder row layout intact and center the folder content block by applying the measured rendered row height to real source rows before the centering helper positions `folder-name-sub`.
- Fix: Avoid the previous Application-column layout experiment and correct the original centering helper instead, so the row no longer sits at the top without disturbing column alignment.
- Regression guard: Cover the legacy flex-layout plus measured source-row-height contract in `docker.modules.js`.


###2026.03.30.04
- Fix: Revert the Docker and VM Application-column layout experiment and restore the pre-`2026.03.29.26` folder row structure after the centering changes caused row distortion and column misalignment.
- Fix: Restore the original Docker folder row centering helper contract in `docker.modules.js`, including the pre-existing CSS gutter pairing for the folder dropdown side.
- Regression guard: Remove the Application-column centering regression test that only covered the reverted experiment and keep the shared Docker layout contract aligned with the restored CSS.


###2026.03.30.03
- Fix: Use the measured visible folder-row height when applying the original Docker `folder-name-sub` centering helper instead of resetting source rows to `0`, so the folder icon, name, and started or stopped status center vertically in the row.
- UX: Keep the original folder-row centering path and adjust those runtime helper lines directly instead of relying on unrelated host-row-only overrides.
- Regression guard: Cover the Docker source-row centering helper contract in `docker.modules.js`.


###2026.03.30.02
