- Fix: Add Docker and VMs runtime preflight diagnostics so unsupported Unraid versions, missing host dependencies, Docker/libvirt probe failures, and active override files surface in a top-of-page troubleshooting banner before the runtime starts.
- Fix: Detect Docker and VM host-table signature drift explicitly, so missing `#docker_containers` / `#docker_list` or `#kvm_table` / `#kvm_list` markup now reports as a named page-structure failure instead of a vague runtime break.
- Quality: Harden server bootstrap with safe host dependency loading plus new runtime preflight regression coverage, keeping Docker/VM troubleshooting visible even when old or broken hosts would previously fatal before the banner loaded.


###2026.03.26.21
- Fix: Roll up the promoted `dev` line since main `2026.03.26.17`, adding top-of-page runtime diagnostics banners on the Docker and VMs pages so bootstrap, request, and render failures no longer fail silently.
- Fix: Restore the page-level Docker and VM `Add Folder` actions by exposing the runtime handler globally, keeping the inline host-page buttons working after update.
- Quality: Extract the shared runtime diagnostics bridge into the common Docker/VM runtime module and expand architecture guards so diagnostics stay visible without tripping the performance ratchet.


###2026.03.26.20
- Fix: Added a top-of-page runtime diagnostics banner on the Docker and VMs pages so bootstrap, request, and render failures now surface with copyable details instead of silently failing.
- Fix: Bound the Docker and VM `Add Folder` page actions onto the live runtime so inline page buttons still work even when the host page expects global handlers.
- Quality: Moved the shared runtime diagnostics bridge into the common runtime module and added architecture guards so Docker and VM runtime failures stay visible without tripping the file-size ratchet.

