###2026.03.24.10
- Fix: Reworked the modern folder settings page to use the proven legacy folder-editor runtime underneath the new chrome, so existing-folder load/save behavior now comes from the same path that already works on the classic editor.
- UX: The new folder settings page is now a true UI overlay on top of the shared form state instead of a second competing bootstrap path, which avoids blank-folder loads when editing existing Docker or VM folders.
- Fix: Modern editor buttons now resolve their actions lazily through the legacy runtime exports, and the legacy runtime now exposes the modern top-bar actions needed by the new chrome.
- Test: Updated folder-editor smoke coverage so modern mode must ship the chrome layer while still relying on the legacy runtime wiring.

###2026.03.24.09
- Fix: Modern folder editor now receives a server-resolved requested-folder bootstrap context, so editing an existing Docker or VM folder can hydrate from the saved record immediately instead of opening as a blank new-folder form.
- Fix: Modern folder editor no longer hard-fails just because `folder.editor.hierarchy.js` is stale or missing; it falls back to an inline hierarchy controller so the form can still load, bind buttons, and populate parent-folder options.
- UX: Existing-folder values are now applied to the new editor as soon as the page boots, before slower runtime lookups finish, which makes the modern form much more resilient during partial loads.
- Fix: Added explicit modern-editor load failure reporting in the in-page validation panel so future bootstrap failures do not silently leave the redesign shell half-loaded.
- Test: Added regression coverage for modern editor bootstrap context emission and the hierarchy-fallback hydration path.

###2026.03.24.08
- Fix: Added a page-version sentinel to Settings, Folder editor, Docker, VMs, and Dashboard so plugin pages force one automatic reload when the installed FolderView Plus version changes during the current browser session.
- UX: This reduces the need for manual `Ctrl+Shift+F5` refreshes after updates by self-healing stale in-memory page shells on the next page load.
- Test: Added security regression coverage so every plugin page must emit the version sentinel along with the no-cache guards and request-token meta tag.


###2026.03.24.07
- Fix: Restored legacy folder editor reset helpers for preview border and chevron colors, so the grouped reset buttons work again on the old form.
- Fix: Legacy folder editor chevron-style normalization now accepts `boxed` and legacy chevron aliases instead of collapsing everything back to `minimal`.
- Fix: Legacy folder editor now reloads and saves chevron style compatibility aliases, so reopening a folder preserves `Boxed` correctly.
- Test: Added regression coverage for legacy editor reset helpers and boxed chevron compatibility on the split legacy runtime.


###2026.03.24.06
- Test: Expanded the no-cache page guard to discover plugin page entrypoints automatically instead of checking only a fixed hardcoded list.
- Quality: Newly added plugin `.page` files must now emit the document no-cache headers, no-cache meta tags, and request-token meta tag or the security regression suite will fail.


###2026.03.24.05
- Fix: Legacy folder settings mode now loads a dedicated pre-redesign editor runtime instead of sharing the redesigned `folder.js` path, so the old form no longer inherits modern editor chrome and mixed save logic.
- Fix: `Folder.page` now boots the modern editor stack only when `folderEditorMode` is `modern`; legacy mode skips the redesign chrome and loads `folder.legacy.js` directly.
- UX: This restores a clean separation between the old and new folder settings pages while the redesigned editor continues behind the opt-in toggle.
- Test: Added page-smoke and security regression coverage for the split legacy/modern editor runtime loading contract.


###2026.03.24.04
- Fix: Folder editor type detection now falls back to the page path, so legacy editor loads still resolve as Docker or VM even when the query string is incomplete or stripped by navigation.
- Fix: Existing-folder editor prefill is now stored in both `sessionStorage` and `localStorage`, and the editor reads either source when recovering the clicked folder record.
- UX: This gives the legacy folder settings page a more robust edit recovery path instead of dropping into a blank new-folder form when one storage/path route fails.
- Test: Added regression coverage for persistent folder-editor prefill storage and the cache-busted redirect helpers.


###2026.03.24.03
