- Refactor: Extracted settings support actions into `folderviewplus.actions-support.js` so the main settings runtime no longer owns the backup, rollback, import/export, diagnostics, and window-action export wall inline.
- Refactor: Extracted shared Docker/VM expanded-state lifecycle and theme/viewport reflow observers into `folder.runtime.state-observers.js`, then rewired both runtimes through controller wrappers instead of duplicating sync timers and DOM lifecycle hooks.
- Refactor: Extracted Docker preview member action handling into `docker.member-menu.js` and folder editor icon upload/request helpers into `folder.editor.icon-api.js` to reduce DOM/event and request plumbing inside `docker.js` and `folder.js`.
- Test: Updated architecture, mobile, security, expanded-state, preview, and UI smoke regressions to follow the extracted module boundaries and keep include-order/browser-compat contracts enforced.


###2026.03.23.11
- Refactor: Extracted the Dashboard quick-rail and layout DOM controller into `dashboard.layout-quickrail.js` so `dashboard.js` no longer owns quick-rail timers, observers, or inline host plumbing directly.
- Quality: Kept Dashboard business logic in `dashboard.js` behind thin controller wrappers while moving quick-rail visibility, alignment, and layout-apply state orchestration into the dedicated module.
- Test: Added regression coverage for Dashboard page load order and updated layout-contract assertions to follow the extracted quick-rail controller boundary.


###2026.03.23.10
- Refactor: Extracted settings table schema and width metadata into `folderviewplus.settings-metadata.js` so the main settings runtime no longer owns the full table contract inline.
- Quality: Centralized dashboard layout metadata, dashboard overflow normalization, and runtime-safe escaping/image sanitization helpers in `folderviewplus.utils.js`, then reused them across Dashboard, Docker, VM, and the folder editor.
- Test: Expanded browser smoke coverage for Dashboard quick-rail layout cycling and extended theme-matrix runtime checks to inspect Docker, VM, and Dashboard surfaces for visibility and contrast regressions.
- Quality: Added a main-branch history guard and wired it into CI, pre-push, and release workflows to catch fresh merge commits before release automation runs.


###2026.03.23.09
- Maintenance: Release main `2026.03.23.09` with the full `dev` rollup since main `2026.03.22.07`, including Dashboard, preview, settings, and packaging improvements.
- Feature: Added a Dashboard widget `Legacy` layout for both Docker and VM widgets so each widget can show native Unraid rows without FolderView Plus grouping.
- Feature: Added per-folder Docker `Preview rows` plus a richer member action sheet for preview and expanded-folder actions.
- UX: Added per-folder chevron style/color controls and adjustable preview border and vertical-bar thickness for better visibility on stock Unraid themes.
- Fix: Rebuilt Docker multi-row previews to resolve clipping, wrapping, spacing, status-text, and action-placement regressions, including truncated counts like `9/9 started`.
- Fix: Reworked Dashboard `Legacy` transitions so they rebuild locally and keep the action rail visible while switching in or out of bypass mode.
- UX: Simplified plugin settings with a fixed action bar, instant-persist table width/layout controls, and cleaner section apply indicators.
- Quality: Hardened branch-aware packaging, manifest/update metadata, release validation, and regression coverage across Dashboard, preview, settings, and runtime paths.


###2026.03.23.08
- Fix: Kept the Dashboard widget action rail visible from the start of `Legacy` view exits instead of waiting for the async widget rebuild to begin.
- Quality: Cleared per-widget `Legacy` transition state on failed or superseded view switches so quick-rail visibility does not get stuck.
- Test: Expanded Dashboard layout regression coverage for early transition-state activation during `Legacy` view switches.


###2026.03.23.07
- Fix: Kept the Dashboard widget action rail visible during `Legacy` view transitions by tracking per-widget layout rebuild state instead of hiding the rail while cards are temporarily absent.
- Quality: Hardened the Dashboard quick-rail visibility logic so it treats local widget rebuilds as an active state rather than a collapsed/empty widget.
- Test: Added regression coverage for transition-in-flight handling in the Dashboard layout runtime.


###2026.03.23.06
- Fix: Reworked Dashboard widget `Legacy` transitions to restore native rows locally instead of forcing a full `loadlist()` refresh, removing the extra delay when cycling in and out of bypass mode.
- Fix: Prevented one widget entering `Legacy` from short-circuiting the other widget's folder render path by scoping dashboard rebuilds to the affected type.
- Test: Expanded dashboard layout regression coverage for the local `Legacy` rerender path and type-scoped widget rebuilds.


